Chapter: EqGenericFields

  cites Foreword chapter Console

 COMPILER-24. A field declared at a TYPE PARAMETER used to be compared by
 POINTER, silently, so two structurally equal values built by different
 routes answered `ne`.

 The join is what failed, not any one function. `emit-eq-op` receives the
 site type carrying the real instantiation, but `resolve-to-sum-with-defs`
 answers the declaration's own formal parameters; and a type parameter
 arrives as a `ConstructedTy` carrying its NAME with no arguments, never as
 a `TypeVar`, which was the only case `subst-field-type` matched. So the
 substitution was a silent no-op for the one case it exists to serve: the
 field kept the parameter's own type, `emit-eq-op` found no arm for it, and
 a word compare on two heap pointers is a pointer comparison.

 Every row builds one side at RUNTIME with `integer-to-text`, so the two
 sides are separate allocations holding equal content. A literal on both
 sides would prove nothing, because a pooled literal compares equal by
 pointer for the wrong reason: `text-control` is the check that the
 instrument itself is honest.

 `concrete-control` is the same shape with the field declared at a concrete
 type. It passed before this fix and must keep passing, so a regression that
 broke instantiation generally would show here rather than hide.

 The RECURSIVE case is COMPILER-43 and is deliberately not asserted here; a
 recursive sum never reaches `emit-eq-op` at all. Its reproducer is
 docs/Test/Active/EqGenericDiscriminator.codex.

Section: Types

  Pair a = | P (a) (a)

  Holder a b = | H (a) (b)

  Plain = | Q (Text) (Text)

Section: Helpers

  yn : Boolean -> Text
  yn (b) = if b then "yes" else "no"

Section: Body

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("text-control     : " & yn ("12" == integer-to-text 12))
    print-line-uni ("concrete-control : " & yn (Q "12" "9" == Q (integer-to-text 12) "9"))
    print-line-uni ("one-param eq     : " & yn (P "12" "9" == P (integer-to-text 12) "9"))
    print-line-uni ("one-param ne     : " & yn (P "12" "9" == P (integer-to-text 13) "9"))
    print-line-uni ("second param     : " & yn (H 7 "12" == H 7 (integer-to-text 12)))
    print-line-uni ("second param ne  : " & yn (H 7 "12" == H 8 (integer-to-text 12)))
  end

